<title>BANGLADESH: BANGLADESH JULY FOREX RESERVES FALL TO $1.62 BLN.</title>
<headline>BANGLADESH JULY FOREX RESERVES FALL TO $1.62 BLN.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh's foreign exchange reserves fell to $1.62 billion at the end of July from $1.72 billion in June, central bank officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The reserves were $1.99 billion in July, 1996.</p>
<p>Foreign exchange reserves (month):</p>
<p>(in billion dollars)</p>
<p>    June	     June	    July 96</p>
<p>    $1.62	    $1.72	   $1.99</p>
</text>
